@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+---
+id: task-001-discount-codes-on-orders
+type: task
+title: "Discount codes on orders"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Discount codes on orders
+
+Request: customers get discount codes in the spring newsletter; an order can take one.
+
+- `SPRING10`: 10 % off the order's items, rounded to the nearest cent (half a cent rounds up).
+- `WELCOME5`: 5.00 EUR off the items, only if the items come to 30.00 EUR or more.
+- One code per order at most; a second code replaces the first.
+- An unknown code, or `WELCOME5` on a smaller order, is refused with an error saying why; the order is unchanged.
+- The discount never touches shipping; free shipping is decided on the items before any discount.
+- API: `OrderBook.applyCode(orderNumber, code)`; `OrderTotals.discountCents` (0 without a code);
+  `totalCents = itemsCents - discountCents + shippingCents`.
+
+Also fixed, because free shipping must be decided on the items correctly: `shippingFor` ignored quantities and
+required strictly more than 50.00 EUR, contrary to its documented "this amount or more".
+
+Done when: tests cover each rule, `npm test` passes, README/CHANGELOG updated.
